# WAVEComp Layout & Styling Rules

## 1. SVG Borders and Lines
- Horizontal separators are inline-SVG React components (`BorderLine`, `Line` in `src/components/`), each rendering `block w-full h-[10px]`. Add new separators the same way.
- Don't render these SVGs via `<img>` or Next `<Image>`: `<Image>` can't serve SVG without `dangerouslyAllowSVG` (intentionally off), and `<img>` triggers `no-img-element` plus an extra fetch.

## 2. Global Padding
- Global horizontal padding is `px-[15px] md:px-[45px]` (15px mobile, 45px desktop). A bare `px-[45px]` breaks mobile.

## 3. Custom Grid System
- This project uses a custom 6-column grid system (`.grid-6`, `.col-n`).
- Keep the `.col-n` utilities inside `@layer utilities { ... }` in `globals.css`; outside that layer Tailwind can't generate responsive variants like `max-[800px]:col-6` or `md:col-3`.
- `md:col-3` paired with `.col-6` means "full width on mobile, half width on desktop".

## 4. WorkCard "Release Date" Alignment
- Inside `WorkCard.tsx`, the `role` text displays as space-between tag pairs. Keep `Release` (or `#Release`) and `Date: [YYYY.MM]` items split with commas in standard arrays passed as `role={roleArray.join(", ")}` so the card correctly justifies them to the left and right corners.
